WEBVTT

00:55.764 --> 00:56.598
"My brother...

00:58.141 --> 01:00.226
I just want my brother to die!"

01:00.310 --> 01:01.770
I just want

01:01.853 --> 01:03.897
my brother to die!

01:04.731 --> 01:06.733
"I just want my brother to die!

01:06.816 --> 01:08.651
I just want my brother to die."

01:08.735 --> 01:10.737
You said that.

01:10.820 --> 01:14.115
You said to Mom every day
that you wanted me to die.

01:14.199 --> 01:16.743
That's why you pushed me into the river
that day.

01:18.953 --> 01:19.996
I shouted for help.

01:20.622 --> 01:23.583
I shouted... I kept crying for help,

01:23.666 --> 01:24.918
but you ran away.

01:25.001 --> 01:26.628
You left me alone in the water
and ran away.

01:27.337 --> 01:30.256
You wanted me dead. Every single day...

01:31.633 --> 01:35.094
- I bet you wanted to kill me.
- No...

01:35.678 --> 01:36.721
Everyone.

01:37.806 --> 01:39.766
Everyone!

01:40.934 --> 01:43.770
He's trying to kill his older brother!

01:45.688 --> 01:47.315
- No.
- Everyone!

01:47.398 --> 01:48.316
No...

01:48.399 --> 01:51.194
He's trying to kill his older brother!

01:52.570 --> 01:55.073
Listen, people!

01:55.156 --> 01:56.241
He is...

01:56.324 --> 01:58.743
- He's trying to kill his older brother!
- No...

01:59.702 --> 02:03.289
Everyone,
He's trying to kill his older brother!

02:03.373 --> 02:07.210
Sang-tae. Do you know the story called
King Donkey Ears?

02:07.293 --> 02:08.795
He's trying to kill his older brother!

02:11.714 --> 02:12.966
Listen, everyone!

02:14.926 --> 02:16.177
He... He's trying to...

02:16.678 --> 02:17.720
Everyone!

02:18.179 --> 02:20.890
Listen up, everyone!

02:21.391 --> 02:23.143
He's trying to kill his older brother!

02:23.226 --> 02:24.644
No...

02:24.727 --> 02:26.729
- Everyone, listen!
- No, that's not true.

02:26.813 --> 02:29.399
- My little brother tried to kill me!
- That's not true.

02:31.276 --> 02:34.487
No, Sang-tae. That's not true.

02:36.739 --> 02:41.077
CHAPTER 10
THE GIRL WHO CRIED WOLF

02:44.831 --> 02:45.915
UNDER SEDATION
DO NOT DISTURB

02:47.167 --> 02:48.376
Did he fall asleep?

02:48.877 --> 02:49.711
Yes.

02:56.801 --> 02:59.220
We gave him sedatives, and he fell asleep.

03:00.597 --> 03:02.348
Why don't you let him stay here
for a while?

03:03.141 --> 03:04.851
I'm not saying he should be hospitalized.

03:05.602 --> 03:07.395
We'll just temporarily
take care of him here.

03:10.148 --> 03:10.982
Okay.

03:17.155 --> 03:18.823
He'll be asleep for a while.

03:20.450 --> 03:23.912
You should go outside and get some air.

04:19.926 --> 04:23.471
Hey, where are you going?

04:25.765 --> 04:27.684
How far are you going to walk?

04:30.478 --> 04:31.854
My feet hurt.

04:33.940 --> 04:34.857
Gang-tae!

04:39.237 --> 04:41.197
I told you not to turn your back on me!

04:56.963 --> 04:57.964
It's your fault

04:59.215 --> 05:01.092
for having such a broad back.

05:04.053 --> 05:04.971
Aren't you hungry?

05:06.472 --> 05:08.766
There's a delicious udon restaurant

05:08.850 --> 05:10.810
- two train stops away from here.
- Ko Mun-yeong.

05:13.938 --> 05:15.231
Stop following me.

05:23.948 --> 05:25.992
But we go hand in hand.
We should be together.

05:29.454 --> 05:30.455
Go home.

05:32.248 --> 05:33.499
I need to be with my brother.

05:36.919 --> 05:38.463
You did nothing wrong.

05:41.632 --> 05:43.301
Your brother just got unlucky

05:43.509 --> 05:45.053
and fell into the river that day.

05:47.138 --> 05:49.932
Gang-tae! Help!

05:50.016 --> 05:51.392
Gang-tae!

05:52.894 --> 05:55.146
You were a coward,
but you weren't malicious.

05:58.232 --> 05:59.442
You ran away, but in the end,

06:00.610 --> 06:02.111
you came back and saved your brother.

06:05.990 --> 06:07.158
You're innocent.

06:11.913 --> 06:12.997
I ran away

06:15.416 --> 06:17.210
because I really

06:20.171 --> 06:21.506
wanted him to die.

06:24.842 --> 06:25.927
Sang-tae knows that.

06:27.345 --> 06:28.346
And

06:29.555 --> 06:30.681
so did you.

06:33.184 --> 06:34.811
What do you know about me?

06:35.311 --> 06:37.355
Who are you to act up like this?

06:38.147 --> 06:39.273
Hypocrite.

06:42.068 --> 06:43.653
There's no way I'm innocent.

06:44.487 --> 06:45.613
So

06:46.197 --> 06:47.824
are you going to sacrifice
your entire life

06:48.199 --> 06:50.535
for your brother
so you can atone for your sin?

06:54.831 --> 06:55.832
Why did you

06:57.125 --> 06:58.376
save me

07:01.170 --> 07:02.672
from the river that day?

07:04.841 --> 07:06.175
You should've just left me to die.

07:08.594 --> 07:09.929
If I had died that day,

07:12.932 --> 07:14.392
I wouldn't have had to live this way.

07:48.176 --> 07:50.261
I kept calling for him.

07:51.762 --> 07:52.805
But he left.

07:54.265 --> 07:56.100
He just abandoned me.

07:58.269 --> 08:00.313
He left me all alone

08:02.190 --> 08:03.691
and left far away.

08:04.192 --> 08:05.443
He tried to kill his brother.

08:06.235 --> 08:07.695
I heard he pushed him into a river.

08:08.779 --> 08:10.990
You really can't tell a book by its cover.

08:12.575 --> 08:14.118
No wonder his smile

08:14.202 --> 08:16.370
always seemed a bit creepy.

08:16.496 --> 08:18.247
I saw it.

08:19.165 --> 08:21.292
- What?
- I could tell

08:21.375 --> 08:23.419
by the look in his eyes.

08:23.836 --> 08:27.590
He's a guy who's cruel enough
to kill someone.

08:27.673 --> 08:29.842
- But he's handsome.
- Ignore her. She's talking gibberish.

08:29.926 --> 08:31.093
Yes, he really is.

08:31.177 --> 08:32.762
So what if he's handsome?

08:34.055 --> 08:36.599
You crazy shaman!

08:36.682 --> 08:38.142
- Jeong-tae!
- Watch what comes out of your mouth!

08:48.694 --> 08:50.238
My gosh.

08:59.330 --> 09:00.206
Wipe your face.

09:02.291 --> 09:04.877
Mr. Joo Jeong-tae was really good

09:05.211 --> 09:07.213
at aiming people with a fire extinguisher.

09:07.296 --> 09:09.799
I guess he really was a firefighter
back in the days.

09:09.882 --> 09:12.009
That stuff is used to put out fire,
not people.

09:12.093 --> 09:13.594
Didn't you hear what he said?

09:14.136 --> 09:16.847
The stuff we said is
what caused this mess.

09:17.598 --> 09:20.768
Let's be careful of what we say
from now on.

09:21.310 --> 09:23.646
Let's not even talk about Mr. Moon.

09:26.107 --> 09:27.024
My gosh.

09:29.443 --> 09:30.903
- Ms. Park.
- Yes?

09:30.987 --> 09:33.864
Here are Ms. Park Ok-ran's recent
counseling records that you asked for.

09:36.534 --> 09:38.869
But why are you interested in her
all of a sudden?

09:40.454 --> 09:44.542
Well, she's been experiencing
severe changes in mood lately.

09:44.625 --> 09:46.544
And her affect seems
very different from usual.

09:46.627 --> 09:47.587
AFFECT: EXPRESSION OF FEELINGS
AND EMOTION

09:47.670 --> 09:50.464
I just want to see
if there's a specific cause to that.

09:50.965 --> 09:52.341
COUNSELING ROOM

09:54.969 --> 09:57.054
Are you getting along okay
at the hospital?

09:57.138 --> 09:58.889
I have a question.

10:01.559 --> 10:02.727
Go ahead.

10:04.437 --> 10:05.605
Did he really try to kill him?

10:06.897 --> 10:07.898
What?

10:08.733 --> 10:10.610
Did the caregiver really try
to kill his brother?

10:15.323 --> 10:19.076
No, I believe there was a misunderstanding
between the two.

10:27.793 --> 10:28.628
Ms. Park.

10:30.838 --> 10:33.049
Why do you think Othello...

10:34.508 --> 10:35.593
killed his wife?

10:39.722 --> 10:40.973
Because of a misunderstanding.

10:53.527 --> 10:55.029
I brought your bag.

11:07.333 --> 11:08.501
Sang-tae, are you sleeping?

11:10.252 --> 11:11.087
Aren't you hungry?

11:13.589 --> 11:15.216
This place feels really empty, doesn't it?

11:15.800 --> 11:18.094
I'll move you to the ward
once there's an empty room.

11:19.011 --> 11:20.805
By any chance, if you want to go home--

11:20.888 --> 11:23.265
No. I don't want to go home.

11:24.392 --> 11:27.144
Okay, you can stay here for a while.

11:29.105 --> 11:31.690
Let me know if you need anything.

11:32.900 --> 11:33.734
Okay?

11:53.045 --> 11:55.798
My gosh, he's been out of reach all day.

11:56.215 --> 11:57.466
This is driving me crazy.

11:58.008 --> 12:00.386
I bet there's one more person
who's having a mental breakdown.

12:00.469 --> 12:01.470
Do you think I should go?

12:01.554 --> 12:03.264
You can't do anything to help Mun-yeong.

12:03.347 --> 12:05.141
No, I was talking about Mr. Moon Sang-tae.

12:05.641 --> 12:06.475
Hey.

12:06.976 --> 12:09.145
God knows when she'll start
writing her next book

12:09.228 --> 12:11.564
now that she got involved in their fight.

12:11.647 --> 12:13.441
But you're worried about
the older brother?

12:13.524 --> 12:14.358
Unbelievable!

12:15.651 --> 12:17.653
You really care about
nothing else but money.

12:18.154 --> 12:19.155
What did you just say?

12:19.905 --> 12:21.824
Your parents gave you an appropriate name.

12:21.907 --> 12:24.285
"Sang-in" means merchant!
You're all about the money!

12:25.703 --> 12:28.414
Then I guess according to your name,
you're always out of luck.

12:29.790 --> 12:32.793
My parents went to a naming center
and paid 300,000 won for my name.

12:32.877 --> 12:35.713
My great-grandfather who fought for our
country's independence gave me my name!

12:36.964 --> 12:38.424
Stop it, you guys.

12:39.008 --> 12:42.261
I'm worried sick because I don't even know
if my friend is dead or alive.

12:42.344 --> 12:44.180
But all you care about is selling books.

12:44.263 --> 12:47.349
If Ko Mun-yeong hadn't convinced him
to go on a trip with her,

12:47.433 --> 12:48.767
none of this would've happened.

12:51.562 --> 12:53.189
It takes two to tango.

12:53.564 --> 12:56.066
He went with her because he wanted to.

12:56.150 --> 12:58.652
He left his brother here all by himself

12:58.736 --> 13:00.696
and spent the night with Mun-yeong.

13:00.779 --> 13:02.698
I bet he went with her
with an ulterior motive.

13:06.285 --> 13:08.412
I really think you guys should shut up.

13:09.288 --> 13:12.333
Ko Mun-yeong is the cause of all this!

13:13.834 --> 13:17.087
Moon Gang-tae is the cunning one!

13:17.171 --> 13:19.048
- Are you serious?
- Seriously?

13:19.131 --> 13:21.175
- Are you kidding me?
- Look who's talking.

13:21.258 --> 13:23.052
Oh, gosh. Did you work out?

13:28.349 --> 13:29.433
Let's eat.

13:30.768 --> 13:31.602
- Okay.
- Okay.

13:49.411 --> 13:51.372
I know they have a lot on their minds.

13:52.164 --> 13:54.542
But I hope they didn't skip their meals.

14:23.487 --> 14:25.489
UNDER SEDATION
DO NOT DISTURB

14:49.847 --> 14:50.890
Sang-tae.

15:02.735 --> 15:04.403
Why did you save me
from the river that day?

15:04.862 --> 15:06.280
You should've just left me to die.

15:06.363 --> 15:07.573
That horrible jerk.

15:37.061 --> 15:39.063
Why is he just sitting there
instead of going inside?

15:44.276 --> 15:48.113
When someone has autism,
it means they shut the door to the world.

15:49.448 --> 15:50.866
Gang-tae is

15:52.326 --> 15:55.329
waiting for Sang-tae
to open that door first.

16:20.854 --> 16:22.815
He's like a trapped ghost.

16:24.900 --> 16:26.819
He can't approach you.

16:27.945 --> 16:29.279
But he can't leave either.

16:30.447 --> 16:32.282
He's just like a ghost that's trapped.

16:37.997 --> 16:39.248
I bet it's really hot in there.

16:40.332 --> 16:42.042
It's driving you crazy, isn't it?

16:44.753 --> 16:45.796
Wait a minute.

16:46.588 --> 16:50.050
How long did it take
for Crown Prince Sado to die

16:50.134 --> 16:51.969
in the rice chest?

16:55.097 --> 16:56.682
I can't remember if he died

16:57.891 --> 16:59.393
due to hunger

17:02.104 --> 17:04.064
or died due to the heat.

17:06.358 --> 17:08.902
You brothers are both

17:09.403 --> 17:10.696
extremely stubborn.

17:11.947 --> 17:14.116
I'll take your brother upstairs.

17:14.700 --> 17:16.994
So come out of there
and get some fresh air.

17:17.077 --> 17:19.079
And go to the bathroom.

17:19.496 --> 17:20.497
My goodness.

17:58.035 --> 17:59.078
Eat this.

18:00.120 --> 18:02.122
This is the best
when you don't have an appetite.

18:07.628 --> 18:09.004
Have you tried a three-legged race?

18:09.588 --> 18:13.050
You know, where each pair have their
adjacent legs bound together and run.

18:16.053 --> 18:18.472
I tried it a couple of times
at my son's school sports event.

18:18.639 --> 18:20.557
But I always ended up falling down first.

18:21.141 --> 18:23.310
So we never got to reach the finish line.

18:26.563 --> 18:28.982
It's like you and your brother
are running a three-legged race.

18:34.363 --> 18:35.322
Do you think

18:37.157 --> 18:39.618
we're both holding each other back?

18:40.202 --> 18:41.245
No.

18:42.746 --> 18:44.164
You're both relying on each other.

18:44.748 --> 18:47.709
As long as one person stays strong
when the other person falls down,

18:48.252 --> 18:49.753
you guys will never fall down together.

18:50.879 --> 18:52.214
Try your best to stay strong.

18:53.382 --> 18:54.216
Who knows?

18:55.551 --> 18:57.302
Sang-tae might be the one
to help you one day.

19:08.814 --> 19:09.690
I thought Sang-tae

19:13.944 --> 19:15.654
had forgotten about everything.

19:18.157 --> 19:20.159
He never once mentioned that day.

19:24.121 --> 19:26.206
So I thought he had erased it
from his mind.

19:26.290 --> 19:28.250
That's what you wanted to believe.

19:29.710 --> 19:33.755
But most people with autism
have really good memory.

19:34.423 --> 19:38.051
They either just try to avoid
their emotions

19:39.595 --> 19:42.598
or express their emotions
a little differently compared to us.

19:45.267 --> 19:46.351
"Avoid"?

19:46.768 --> 19:48.604
You shouldn't avoid it.
Just face it head-on.

19:51.106 --> 19:52.357
Come back to work.

19:53.275 --> 19:54.902
Ms. Lee A-reum's ex-husband told me

19:54.985 --> 19:58.739
he's going to drop all charges
after I blackmailed him a little.

19:59.364 --> 20:01.491
I suspended you for a few days,

20:01.575 --> 20:02.910
so that's more than enough.

20:05.621 --> 20:07.873
- Is that really--
- I need you back because the guy

20:07.956 --> 20:10.459
who's doing your job is terrible at it.
Maybe I should fire him.

20:15.505 --> 20:16.506
That hurts!

20:16.590 --> 20:18.133
Ms. Park! Ms. Nam!

20:19.259 --> 20:22.346
Hey, stop. Jeong-tae.
You shouldn't bite people.

20:22.971 --> 20:24.223
You're not a dog or a crocodile.

20:24.306 --> 20:26.183
- My gosh, please stop.
- That's enough.

20:26.266 --> 20:28.352
It really hurts! Let me go!

20:28.852 --> 20:29.811
Mr. Moon.

20:35.692 --> 20:36.526
Gang-tae.

20:38.362 --> 20:39.279
Gang-tae.

20:41.573 --> 20:43.742
He refused to take his medicine.

20:43.909 --> 20:45.827
He's a patient.
He should take his medicine.

20:46.578 --> 20:48.413
You can't force patients
to take their medicine.

20:48.997 --> 20:50.999
He did it on purpose.

20:51.083 --> 20:54.127
He lured my fingers near his mouth
so he could bite them.

20:55.212 --> 20:57.130
- Why would he do that?
- I don't know.

20:57.214 --> 20:58.131
He says I'm the problem.

20:58.215 --> 21:01.218
He says it's because I told everyone
that you and Ms. Ko are getting married...

21:05.973 --> 21:08.850
I should've stitched up your mouth,
not your hand.

21:16.108 --> 21:18.068
JAE-SU

21:22.614 --> 21:24.616
So this is how it feels
to love someone unrequitedly.

21:28.161 --> 21:29.871
When you ignored my calls,

21:30.539 --> 21:32.582
I was so worried
that I got extremely angry.

21:33.583 --> 21:37.212
But now that I see you,
it's hard to be angry at you.

21:39.423 --> 21:40.882
I warned you, didn't I?

21:41.925 --> 21:43.343
I told you to stay away from Ko Mun-yeong.

21:44.970 --> 21:48.807
I told you to constantly remind yourself
with that scar she gave you.

21:58.108 --> 21:59.151
Jae-su.

22:03.405 --> 22:04.364
I...

22:07.200 --> 22:08.410
woke up from my dream.

22:19.588 --> 22:21.173
I should've focused on my brother.

22:25.844 --> 22:27.471
But I dared to dream an impossible dream.

22:32.392 --> 22:34.102
I should've known my place.

22:40.525 --> 22:42.486
I dreamed the impossible dream.

23:32.202 --> 23:33.453
My gosh.

23:34.538 --> 23:38.041
I brought all your favorite toppings.

23:40.085 --> 23:41.753
You should eat this while it's warm.

23:43.046 --> 23:44.339
It looks so delicious.

23:45.841 --> 23:47.134
It smells amazing.

23:58.353 --> 23:59.396
Oh, gosh.

24:00.522 --> 24:02.607
I shouldn't leave the restaurant empty
for too long.

24:03.316 --> 24:05.986
I should go back and sell a lot of pizzas.

24:06.695 --> 24:07.946
I don't even have a part-timer.

24:08.655 --> 24:10.782
I bet it'll feel great if I come back

24:10.866 --> 24:12.701
and see an empty box.

24:45.609 --> 24:47.402
KO MUN-YEONG

24:51.531 --> 24:53.658
GANG-TAE

24:57.370 --> 24:59.915
OK PSYCHIATRIC HOSPITAL

25:20.685 --> 25:22.270
Look at you. You look so worn out.

25:23.897 --> 25:26.608
You look like a dried jujube seed.

25:28.693 --> 25:31.112
- Why are you here?
- You haven't been home in a while,

25:31.196 --> 25:32.697
so I brought you your underwear.

25:33.698 --> 25:35.200
Briefs, boxers, thongs, and mesh.

25:35.283 --> 25:37.160
I don't know your taste,
so I brought everything.

25:37.661 --> 25:38.495
Follow me.

25:39.829 --> 25:41.790
- I need to--
- Okay, I'll take care of your report.

25:44.626 --> 25:45.460
Bye, guys.

25:47.337 --> 25:48.505
See? They're dating, right?

25:49.130 --> 25:50.382
She even brought his underwear,

25:50.757 --> 25:52.008
so there's no doubt about it.

26:32.090 --> 26:34.050
"The Murder of the Witch of the West

26:34.718 --> 26:35.969
by Do Hui-jae."

26:47.230 --> 26:49.858
THE LITTLE BROTHER KILLS HIS BIG BROTHER

27:29.564 --> 27:31.107
I thought about it,

27:31.358 --> 27:32.817
and I think this is for the best.

27:34.402 --> 27:36.946
It's time for you to stop playing hostage.

27:39.032 --> 27:39.866
"Hostage"?

27:42.202 --> 27:45.747
I don't want you to spend your entire life

27:45.955 --> 27:47.040
taking care of your brother.

27:51.044 --> 27:52.629
I know you want to live with me.

27:53.755 --> 27:54.964
You want me in your arms,

27:55.382 --> 27:57.175
and you want to have fun with me.

28:01.179 --> 28:02.013
No.

28:02.722 --> 28:04.474
Your mouth can tell lies.

28:06.393 --> 28:07.352
But those eyes

28:08.478 --> 28:09.562
cannot.

28:14.192 --> 28:15.026
I...

28:17.570 --> 28:18.988
woke up from my dream.

28:20.365 --> 28:21.324
What?

28:21.408 --> 28:22.534
It's my fault.

28:24.577 --> 28:25.620
I...

28:27.122 --> 28:28.581
should've focused on my brother.

28:29.416 --> 28:31.584
He should've been my all.

28:33.294 --> 28:34.546
But I was distracted by you.

28:37.382 --> 28:39.175
I never should've stopped you
that day we met again.

28:40.176 --> 28:42.887
I should've avoided you
when you started talking about destiny.

28:44.139 --> 28:44.973
What we have

28:47.183 --> 28:48.309
is an ill-fated relationship.

28:53.356 --> 28:54.733
Stop putting on an act.

28:55.900 --> 28:57.694
You told me I make you smile.

28:58.111 --> 28:59.487
So there's no way we're ill-fated.

29:00.280 --> 29:01.531
Please do me a favor.

29:04.451 --> 29:05.577
Stay out

29:06.703 --> 29:08.037
of my life.

29:11.082 --> 29:13.042
You promised not to leave me.

29:13.668 --> 29:15.003
- Was that--
- Yes.

29:15.128 --> 29:16.129
It was all bullshit.

29:17.255 --> 29:19.382
It was my first time having fun,
so I got too excited

29:20.300 --> 29:21.718
and just said whatever.

29:23.386 --> 29:24.471
My brother

29:25.930 --> 29:27.640
is already a handful.

29:30.643 --> 29:33.062
I'm already having a hard time
bearing with him, so please...

29:34.981 --> 29:35.899
Please...

29:39.861 --> 29:41.863
Please stop stirring up my miserable life.

29:44.073 --> 29:44.991
And get lost.

29:48.536 --> 29:49.662
You're lying.

29:52.123 --> 29:53.583
Remember what you told me last time?

29:55.460 --> 29:56.920
When I told you to get lost,

29:57.295 --> 29:59.506
you told me it sounded like
I was asking you not to leave.

30:03.009 --> 30:04.260
What you just said

30:07.889 --> 30:09.182
sounded like you want me

30:10.016 --> 30:11.226
to hold onto you.

30:25.949 --> 30:27.033
Don't go.

30:31.621 --> 30:32.539
No.

30:34.415 --> 30:35.250
You were like

30:36.459 --> 30:38.336
a firecracker to me.

30:39.504 --> 30:40.839
A one-time event.

30:42.006 --> 30:43.925
I had my fun, so it's time for you

30:46.845 --> 30:48.680
to get out of my life.

31:15.290 --> 31:17.375
I'm not a firecracker! I'm a bomb!

31:18.251 --> 31:19.752
I don't disappear once I explode!

31:20.378 --> 31:22.255
I blow up and kill everyone!

34:21.350 --> 34:23.561
Then stay there until the doors open.

34:23.644 --> 34:24.854
"Until the doors open"?

34:26.064 --> 34:28.483
Am I a stone sculpture or what?

34:28.691 --> 34:31.986
Making sure the author is well and healthy
is one of your main duties.

34:32.278 --> 34:33.696
Then come here and do it yourself.

34:34.489 --> 34:36.991
How dare you? I'm a busy man,

34:37.116 --> 34:38.743
whereas you have nothing to do.

34:45.500 --> 34:48.086
If you're going to keep treating me
like a worthless surplus,

34:48.753 --> 34:49.587
I'd rather

34:51.380 --> 34:52.799
- quit.
- Oh, gosh.

34:53.299 --> 34:54.926
- Ju-ri.
- Hello?

34:56.427 --> 34:57.470
Mr. Lee?

35:01.140 --> 35:02.141
I hope you go bankrupt.

35:07.647 --> 35:08.981
He already did.

35:18.282 --> 35:19.867
- Heading out to work?
- Yes.

35:21.160 --> 35:22.787
Let's go. I'll give you a ride.

35:22.870 --> 35:24.997
No, it's only a short bus ride away.

35:25.081 --> 35:27.875
- Just finish your breakfast.
- No, I'm done.

35:28.751 --> 35:30.586
I just need to put those away.

35:31.712 --> 35:34.507
I have some time
before my appointment anyway,

35:35.091 --> 35:36.592
so I'll drop you off on the way.

35:38.636 --> 35:39.804
Let me give you a ride.

35:46.185 --> 35:47.812
Let's see what we can listen to.

35:50.982 --> 35:52.275
Are you going somewhere today?

35:53.609 --> 35:57.738
Yes, I have to go to Seoul
to attend a seminar for book publishers.

35:58.239 --> 36:00.116
I need to show the industry people

36:00.199 --> 36:02.034
that I, Lee Sang-in, am still alive.

36:02.118 --> 36:04.162
And I thought I should
do some business as well.

36:09.292 --> 36:10.543
This is a classic car, you know.

36:14.547 --> 36:17.175
Hey, what's wrong with you today?

36:17.258 --> 36:20.469
Why are they both going bonkers?

36:25.349 --> 36:26.434
Hey.

36:27.018 --> 36:29.270
- I think the heater is on.
- What?

36:29.353 --> 36:30.313
The heater.

36:32.273 --> 36:35.693
Jeez, is it because of the hot weather?
What is wrong with my car?

36:37.445 --> 36:39.655
We'll be okay, right?

36:39.739 --> 36:43.951
Yes, of course. It's still no problem

36:44.285 --> 36:46.370
to drive the car...

36:54.212 --> 36:55.630
Be safe, Ju-ri.

36:57.256 --> 36:58.966
Please take good care of her, sir.

37:07.850 --> 37:09.977
It was the perfect chance
to spend some one-on-one time.

37:12.688 --> 37:14.190
My wallet. No, my wallet!

37:43.803 --> 37:44.929
Mom?

37:47.181 --> 37:48.057
It's the Mom.

37:50.101 --> 37:53.271
It's Dooly's mom. A Brachiosaurus!

37:54.272 --> 37:56.232
- Hi!
- Hi. My gosh!

37:56.899 --> 37:59.235
Brachiosaurus. It's huge!

38:01.404 --> 38:06.158
Dooly is a ceratosaurus.
He's a ceratosaurus.

38:06.242 --> 38:07.702
Look, here.

38:07.785 --> 38:09.412
He's a carnivore.

38:09.495 --> 38:13.249
And Dooly's mom... Dooly's mom.

38:13.833 --> 38:14.834
Look, right here.

38:14.917 --> 38:17.837
Dooly's mom is a brachiosaurus,
a herbivore.

38:17.920 --> 38:22.717
They have nostrils on top of the head.
It is one of their main characteristics.

38:22.800 --> 38:23.718
Hang on.

38:24.302 --> 38:26.679
They're mom and son.
How could they be different species?

38:26.762 --> 38:27.596
Right.

38:30.933 --> 38:33.477
There's a secret behind Dooly's birth.

38:33.561 --> 38:35.521
- Really?
- Yes.

38:35.771 --> 38:38.899
Dooly's mom was a stepmom.

38:38.983 --> 38:40.693
I mean, fake. She was a fake mom.

38:40.776 --> 38:45.448
Dooly's real mom lost the egg
before Dooly could hatch.

38:45.531 --> 38:48.451
This brachiosaurus found the egg,
hatched it,

38:48.534 --> 38:50.077
and raised Dooly by herself.

38:50.161 --> 38:55.207
That's the speculation made
by the fans of the cartoon like myself.

38:56.167 --> 38:58.627
So, she was a good mom
even though she was a fake mom.

38:58.711 --> 39:00.463
That's right. Anything fake is bad,

39:02.381 --> 39:03.799
but all moms are good.

39:05.801 --> 39:07.762
Was your mom also a good person?

39:11.557 --> 39:14.477
She was a good mom to me,
but a bad one to Gang-tae.

39:16.145 --> 39:17.938
Dooly...

39:22.526 --> 39:23.361
Here.

39:30.076 --> 39:33.037
Stop staring at the food
and dig in already.

39:34.121 --> 39:35.122
Okay.

39:35.664 --> 39:36.874
Thank you for this.

39:44.799 --> 39:47.301
They say you must be kind
to people you hate.

39:47.635 --> 39:49.637
I wholeheartedly agree with that saying.

39:51.931 --> 39:53.307
I hate you.

39:53.641 --> 39:56.060
That's why I cooked up this feast for you.

39:56.644 --> 39:58.312
You rejected my daughter,

39:58.396 --> 40:00.398
and you're now head over heels
for another girl.

40:00.523 --> 40:01.816
How could I not hate you?

40:03.401 --> 40:05.194
"Should I tell them to move out?

40:05.820 --> 40:08.948
Not seeing him around
will help her forget him and move on."

40:09.448 --> 40:10.908
I ask myself all the time.

40:14.954 --> 40:17.289
Would you like us to move out?

40:20.334 --> 40:21.710
I don't think

40:22.294 --> 40:25.297
I can sleep worry-free at night
after kicking you guys out, so no.

40:28.008 --> 40:30.136
I'll take Sang-tae home today,

40:30.719 --> 40:33.305
so just focus on
pulling yourself together.

40:40.563 --> 40:41.772
Thank you.

40:41.856 --> 40:43.441
You don't need to thank me.

40:44.567 --> 40:46.444
If you're not going to be my son-in-law,

40:46.819 --> 40:49.238
you should just be born as my son
in your next life.

40:51.323 --> 40:53.909
You can be a good son all your life
and repay me then.

41:01.625 --> 41:03.169
But I don't want to be born again.

41:03.669 --> 41:05.171
Don't be so difficult.

41:06.172 --> 41:07.631
Eat up, will you?

41:17.057 --> 41:18.642
Brachiosaurus.

41:18.726 --> 41:20.978
She doesn't have a teardrop.

41:21.061 --> 41:23.481
However, I'll name her
"Teary without tears."

41:23.564 --> 41:25.900
Teary without tears.

41:27.318 --> 41:30.779
I'm happy. I'm so happy!

41:45.836 --> 41:47.004
You'll come home today, right?

41:52.426 --> 41:53.802
Come home for dinner.

41:54.512 --> 41:56.138
And make up with Sang-tae.

41:58.057 --> 41:59.767
He had a big meal, and I even saw him

41:59.850 --> 42:01.769
having a lengthy conversation
with Ms. Park.

42:03.270 --> 42:05.231
That means he's not angry anymore, right?

42:07.608 --> 42:10.277
You know, there's that thing
we always say to the patients.

42:11.487 --> 42:13.989
"If you want to make
the people around you happy,

42:14.907 --> 42:16.742
you must find your own happiness first."

42:19.703 --> 42:22.873
Being selfish isn't always a bad thing.

42:24.083 --> 42:28.420
Try to only think about your happiness
when things are too stressful.

42:30.339 --> 42:31.549
It's okay to do that.

42:42.977 --> 42:44.061
Then,

42:46.438 --> 42:47.690
can I

42:50.609 --> 42:53.821
ask you for a selfish favor?

43:07.918 --> 43:09.044
DOOLY THE LITTLE DINOSAUR

43:25.144 --> 43:27.813
Come home at once, or I'll wipe out
all these Dooly VHS tapes.

43:31.859 --> 43:34.361
YOU'LL BE IN BIG TROUBLE
IF YOU DON'T COME HOME

43:45.372 --> 43:47.958
Damn it. He's ignoring me again.

43:56.300 --> 43:58.719
I have a fever. I'm sick as a dog.

43:59.345 --> 44:00.679
Pick up some fever reducer for me.

44:05.351 --> 44:07.853
Damn it. He's still ignoring me.

44:16.487 --> 44:17.655
I'm freaking starving...

44:22.534 --> 44:24.286
This was here.

44:34.171 --> 44:36.799
Sang-tae will stay with us at home
for a little while.

44:37.675 --> 44:39.301
He asked me to bring his bare essentials.

44:40.427 --> 44:41.387
"Home"?

44:44.682 --> 44:46.141
So, this wasn't his "home" after all?

44:56.151 --> 44:57.444
MALA BEEF ON RICE

45:30.436 --> 45:32.688
THE LITTLE BROTHER KILLS HIS BIG BROTHER

45:58.505 --> 46:01.216
Sang-tae, I'm coming in.

46:50.307 --> 46:51.141
Sang-tae.

46:53.519 --> 46:55.020
Are you going to keep avoiding me?

46:59.650 --> 47:01.068
Forgive me, please.

47:02.945 --> 47:04.238
I'm sorry.

47:08.116 --> 47:09.243
For what?

47:11.745 --> 47:13.539
What are you sorry for?

47:14.122 --> 47:15.457
What are you apologizing for?

47:24.675 --> 47:26.385
For running away

47:29.388 --> 47:30.722
when you fell into the water.

47:35.435 --> 47:36.520
And for saying

47:39.314 --> 47:41.525
that I wished you were dead.

47:43.151 --> 47:44.653
That was such a mean thing to say.

47:48.949 --> 47:50.033
Also, for wishing...

47:55.330 --> 47:56.582
For wishing

47:57.958 --> 48:00.794
that I had a normal brother
like other kids.

48:02.170 --> 48:03.922
For wishing that often.

48:10.262 --> 48:11.430
Just... For everything.

48:13.557 --> 48:15.309
I'm sorry for everything.

48:18.353 --> 48:19.354
I'm sorry.

48:22.024 --> 48:23.150
Forgive me.

48:24.151 --> 48:24.985
I'm sorry.

48:26.820 --> 48:27.654
I...

48:52.262 --> 48:53.639
I'm sorry.

48:55.807 --> 48:57.225
Don't abandon me.

49:02.439 --> 49:03.940
Don't leave me, Sang-tae.

49:07.486 --> 49:08.695
I'm sorry for everything.

49:27.589 --> 49:30.175
Don't abandon me.

49:34.513 --> 49:35.597
I'm sorry.

49:39.976 --> 49:42.229
Don't abandon me.

49:44.356 --> 49:45.440
I'm sorry.

49:46.316 --> 49:47.567
I'm really sorry.

49:49.194 --> 49:50.612
I'm sorry...

49:51.655 --> 49:53.990
Don't cry.

50:04.918 --> 50:05.919
Don't cry.

50:07.212 --> 50:08.505
Don't cry.

50:25.397 --> 50:26.606
I'm leaving.

50:30.861 --> 50:33.238
Hey, did you have dinner?

50:36.283 --> 50:37.993
I have no food to give you,
but there's wine.

50:44.499 --> 50:46.084
I drove here though.

50:47.377 --> 50:48.295
So what?

50:52.883 --> 50:54.426
Fine, I'll take a taxi home.

51:08.148 --> 51:09.691
Are you no longer afraid of me?

51:10.734 --> 51:11.651
I still am.

51:13.111 --> 51:14.529
I'm afraid of you,

51:15.530 --> 51:16.573
and I hate you.

51:20.994 --> 51:22.037
I'm also jealous.

51:44.935 --> 51:46.853
I'm your big brother.

51:48.772 --> 51:49.773
That's right.

51:50.440 --> 51:52.025
I'm your little brother.

51:52.275 --> 51:53.276
You're mine.

51:53.652 --> 51:56.363
Moon Gang-tae belongs to Moon Sang-tae.

52:00.367 --> 52:01.368
Yes.

52:03.119 --> 52:04.287
I'm all yours.

52:06.540 --> 52:08.291
I like you.

52:11.962 --> 52:13.338
We only met today,

52:13.421 --> 52:15.757
but I like you so much.

52:17.509 --> 52:18.760
I like you so much.

52:25.684 --> 52:27.060
Sweet dreams.

52:38.113 --> 52:41.199
I like you too, Sang-tae.

52:57.632 --> 52:59.175
I see that you can drink.

53:06.349 --> 53:08.018
Let me slap you in the face.

53:08.894 --> 53:12.522
- What?
- I said, let me slap you in the face!

53:17.402 --> 53:18.695
You see,

53:19.237 --> 53:21.531
you are the biggest bitch

53:22.407 --> 53:24.409
in the entire universe.

53:25.035 --> 53:26.494
When we were little,

53:26.578 --> 53:29.039
you harassed my friends

53:29.623 --> 53:32.042
and made me an outcast.

53:32.626 --> 53:36.755
Then you even stole the guy
I have feelings for.

53:39.382 --> 53:41.843
Do you find joy
out of seeing me left all alone?

53:42.802 --> 53:45.889
You stole the one thing I wanted,
knowing I have nothing.

53:47.223 --> 53:49.225
Happy now? You bitch.

53:51.645 --> 53:53.188
You obnoxious bitch.

53:53.939 --> 53:55.607
You're so damn mean!

53:58.652 --> 54:00.695
- You're cute.
- Yes, that's right.

54:01.237 --> 54:02.489
I'm so freaking cute.

54:03.031 --> 54:06.826
When I'm this cute,

54:06.910 --> 54:09.204
why does Gang-tae only like you?

54:12.290 --> 54:13.291
Because I'm pretty?

54:18.588 --> 54:20.006
Screw you.

54:24.177 --> 54:25.261
You little...

54:51.037 --> 54:52.414
One, two, three.

54:53.832 --> 54:55.750
Smile. Don't cry.

55:01.923 --> 55:02.799
Smile.

55:19.274 --> 55:20.442
Ju-ri!

55:21.026 --> 55:21.860
Mun-yeong!

55:26.031 --> 55:27.073
Ju-ri?

55:27.866 --> 55:30.410
- Ju-ri, wake up.
- What? Damn it.

55:33.455 --> 55:34.873
She's just drunk, right?

55:35.373 --> 55:36.833
Don't tell me you hit her.

55:36.916 --> 55:38.460
I almost did,

55:39.127 --> 55:40.628
but she passed out before I could.

55:41.379 --> 55:43.173
How much did she drink?

55:45.592 --> 55:48.219
She's not looking good.
I should carry her on my back.

55:49.596 --> 55:50.513
Do you like her?

55:50.597 --> 55:51.556
Yes.

55:52.682 --> 55:54.142
Who do you like more? Me or her?

55:55.060 --> 55:56.686
What's with you? You're scaring me.

55:56.770 --> 55:58.938
Answer my question. Who do you like more?

56:01.107 --> 56:02.108
Well...

56:02.609 --> 56:04.861
I like you both, in different ways.

56:04.944 --> 56:05.945
That wasn't the question.

56:06.529 --> 56:08.615
Who comes first? And who comes second?

56:13.161 --> 56:14.079
Mun-yeong.

56:15.747 --> 56:17.207
When you're talking about people,

56:18.208 --> 56:21.127
you should never number them like that.

56:22.754 --> 56:26.174
You can cherish and care about people

56:27.175 --> 56:28.384
in different ways.

56:29.219 --> 56:30.845
Think about the different kinds of yellow,

56:30.929 --> 56:33.348
such as vivid yellow,
mustard yellow, and dull yellow.

56:33.431 --> 56:36.392
Even the same color can take
different names depending on its chroma.

56:36.643 --> 56:38.645
The same goes for human emotions,

56:38.853 --> 56:40.146
such as affection.

56:41.272 --> 56:43.775
Fondness, hatred,

56:43.983 --> 56:45.902
love, friendship, and lust.

56:47.070 --> 56:48.988
They are like a rainbow.

56:50.490 --> 56:52.617
But when they're mixed together,

56:53.118 --> 56:54.702
they turn jet black.

56:58.706 --> 57:00.542
You probably got used to living
with those guys.

57:02.877 --> 57:05.922
But how do you feel now that you're alone?

57:11.636 --> 57:12.720
I'm just

57:15.473 --> 57:16.391
bored.

57:18.143 --> 57:19.894
I get sudden bouts of irritability,

57:21.563 --> 57:23.106
and I feel colder at night.

57:25.483 --> 57:26.734
I also get hungry more often.

57:28.987 --> 57:31.448
There's only one way to explain
all those emotions.

57:31.531 --> 57:33.450
Do you know what that is?

57:50.592 --> 57:51.676
You miss him.

57:57.223 --> 57:58.433
I miss him.

58:02.604 --> 58:03.771
I miss him.

58:08.443 --> 58:09.277
I miss him.

58:12.864 --> 58:13.948
I miss him.

58:23.750 --> 58:24.834
I miss him.

58:38.890 --> 58:40.225
Where's my phone?

58:41.100 --> 58:41.935
My phone.

58:43.895 --> 58:44.771
Where did my phone go?

58:45.146 --> 58:46.356
Gosh, where is it?

58:47.941 --> 58:49.943
- My phone...
- Here you go.

58:51.069 --> 58:52.028
Thanks.

58:53.613 --> 58:57.951
Well, I hope I didn't make any mistakes
last night.

58:58.076 --> 58:59.410
No, not at all.

59:00.119 --> 59:04.082
You threw up twice in Mr. Lee's clunker,

59:04.165 --> 59:05.959
but it's a great excuse to scrap the car,

59:06.084 --> 59:07.460
so don't worry about it at all.

59:11.339 --> 59:12.423
Want some?

01:00:00.221 --> 01:00:02.432
Is your stomach okay?

01:00:04.475 --> 01:00:06.769
- Pardon?
- Are you not hungover?

01:00:08.605 --> 01:00:09.480
No.

01:00:12.275 --> 01:00:14.068
Why are you suddenly
talking so casually to me?

01:00:14.652 --> 01:00:15.486
What?

01:00:34.714 --> 01:00:35.757
I can finally breathe.

01:00:36.341 --> 01:00:38.259
- Where's Ju-ri?
- I got her.

01:00:38.343 --> 01:00:39.844
Just get your stuff from the trunk.

01:00:48.061 --> 01:00:50.188
All right, Ju-ri.

01:00:51.856 --> 01:00:53.316
Come on.

01:00:55.568 --> 01:00:56.402
Moon Gang-tae.

01:00:57.070 --> 01:01:00.615
Come on, Ju-ri. Let's go home.

01:01:01.699 --> 01:01:02.992
Did she drink a lot?

01:01:03.076 --> 01:01:05.161
You piece of...

01:01:05.244 --> 01:01:08.414
All right. No more swearing, please.
My ears are about to rot.

01:01:12.543 --> 01:01:14.128
You sent me there on purpose, didn't you?

01:01:15.797 --> 01:01:18.341
So that Ko Mun-yeong and I can make up.

01:01:19.967 --> 01:01:22.011
I bet you were worried
she'd be lonely all by herself.

01:01:23.096 --> 01:01:24.639
Isn't that why you sent me there?

01:01:25.723 --> 01:01:27.558
You jerk.

01:01:28.142 --> 01:01:30.937
Do you not know
that I have feelings for you?

01:01:31.979 --> 01:01:33.773
Do you know or not?

01:01:34.524 --> 01:01:37.735
Quiet down, please. You'll wake up
everyone in the neighborhood.

01:01:39.946 --> 01:01:43.616
You said it's okay to be selfish
when things are too stressful.

01:01:49.372 --> 01:01:51.541
Am I... Do you think I'm a pushover?

01:01:56.879 --> 01:01:59.674
By the way, why do you keep
talking so casually to me?

01:01:59.757 --> 01:02:00.675
Hey!

01:02:01.384 --> 01:02:04.178
Mun-yeong and I are friends.

01:02:04.929 --> 01:02:05.763
Okay?

01:02:06.848 --> 01:02:09.267
So why is it that
when you're talking to her... "Hey!"

01:02:10.560 --> 01:02:11.894
You call her like that,

01:02:12.520 --> 01:02:16.774
while you always talk so politely to me?

01:02:16.858 --> 01:02:18.776
What the heck? You jerk!

01:02:20.987 --> 01:02:22.029
Just talk casually to me.

01:02:23.865 --> 01:02:25.992
Just do as I say, you jerk!

01:02:29.620 --> 01:02:30.621
Okay.

01:02:39.130 --> 01:02:39.964
Thanks.

01:02:48.181 --> 01:02:51.309
Are you not feeling well?

01:02:51.893 --> 01:02:54.312
I'm fine. I'm just tired.

01:03:21.255 --> 01:03:23.090
KO MUN-YEONG

01:03:29.013 --> 01:03:31.307
It's so hot. Can't they turn up
the air conditioner?

01:03:31.933 --> 01:03:34.143
You're hot too, right?
You're covered in sweat.

01:03:34.644 --> 01:03:37.230
- Yes, it's pretty hot today.
- Hold on.

01:03:41.359 --> 01:03:44.028
Jeez, you're burning up.
You feel as hot as a heating pad.

01:03:44.362 --> 01:03:45.780
Are you feeling under the weather?

01:03:46.781 --> 01:03:48.032
I guess the heat got to me.

01:04:03.756 --> 01:04:04.841
Goodness.

01:04:05.842 --> 01:04:08.761
Look at you swearing at me nonstop
as soon as you pick up the phone.

01:04:08.970 --> 01:04:11.222
You were obviously waiting
for someone else's call.

01:04:13.599 --> 01:04:14.642
Mun-yeong.

01:04:15.601 --> 01:04:18.604
I'll treat you to dinner
at a fancy restaurant today.

01:04:19.188 --> 01:04:20.690
Let's have some beef.

01:04:22.483 --> 01:04:25.570
We should slice some steaks.
It's been way too long.

01:04:26.779 --> 01:04:28.781
"Why"? What do you think?

01:04:29.532 --> 01:04:30.950
Today is

01:04:32.118 --> 01:04:34.287
that day, you know. It's that day.

01:04:54.015 --> 01:04:55.141
Does he like the Mom?

01:04:59.145 --> 01:05:00.438
Dooly's mom.

01:05:00.646 --> 01:05:02.189
I gave it to Sang-tae as a gift.

01:05:06.235 --> 01:05:08.154
Thank you for looking out for him.

01:05:09.155 --> 01:05:10.156
Did you know?

01:05:10.948 --> 01:05:12.617
Dooly's mom was actually
not his birth mom.

01:05:16.037 --> 01:05:19.498
Sang-tae is very selective about
who he shares that with.

01:05:20.833 --> 01:05:23.544
Sang-tae and I have gotten quite close.

01:05:25.796 --> 01:05:27.131
By the way,

01:05:28.841 --> 01:05:31.135
do you know if he's close
to Ms. Park Ok-ran, the patient?

01:05:34.597 --> 01:05:35.640
No.

01:05:36.599 --> 01:05:37.433
Why do you ask?

01:05:38.809 --> 01:05:40.269
I was just curious.

01:05:41.604 --> 01:05:45.107
Try to keep a watchful eye on her
during your shifts.

01:05:46.192 --> 01:05:47.777
She's been quite unstable.

01:06:38.369 --> 01:06:40.037
THE MURDER OF THE WITCH OF THE WEST

01:06:44.250 --> 01:06:48.212
I feel as though she's intentionally
trying to provoke other patients.

01:06:52.508 --> 01:06:53.592
That song.

01:06:54.635 --> 01:06:56.012
Did you just hum the song?

01:07:07.231 --> 01:07:08.065
Why?

01:07:09.316 --> 01:07:10.526
Are you going to kill me again?

01:07:16.198 --> 01:07:18.534
Die. Just die!

01:07:18.617 --> 01:07:19.994
Why are you being like this?

01:07:20.828 --> 01:07:21.912
Help!

01:07:21.996 --> 01:07:24.457
- Help--
- You can't fool me anymore, you monster!

01:07:25.458 --> 01:07:26.417
- Help!
- Die.

01:07:26.500 --> 01:07:29.003
- You monster!
- Help me!

01:07:29.086 --> 01:07:30.880
- Mr. Ko!
- Let go!

01:07:31.380 --> 01:07:34.508
Let go of me! I must kill her!

01:07:34.800 --> 01:07:36.677
If not, I will die!

01:07:36.761 --> 01:07:38.637
- Please calm down.
- I said, I'll die!

01:07:38.721 --> 01:07:39.847
Calm down, please.

01:07:39.930 --> 01:07:43.225
- Calm down.
- I'll die if I don't kill her. I'll die!

01:07:47.605 --> 01:07:49.190
I have to kill her!

01:07:50.149 --> 01:07:51.859
I must kill that woman.

01:07:52.401 --> 01:07:55.404
That day,
I should've killed Mun-yeong too.

01:07:56.363 --> 01:07:59.992
All monsters must be killed!

01:08:03.329 --> 01:08:04.413
No!

01:08:06.040 --> 01:08:08.793
Your daughter is not a monster.

01:08:13.380 --> 01:08:15.841
She is not a monster.

01:08:17.843 --> 01:08:19.303
If you don't kill her,

01:08:20.387 --> 01:08:21.555
you will die.

01:08:29.939 --> 01:08:31.774
So, you were just reading.

01:08:31.857 --> 01:08:34.902
Mr. Ko suddenly came up to you
and started choking you?

01:08:36.570 --> 01:08:37.530
For no reason?

01:08:39.907 --> 01:08:40.991
Yes, that's right.

01:08:43.202 --> 01:08:44.203
He called me

01:08:45.246 --> 01:08:46.455
a monster.

01:08:47.540 --> 01:08:48.541
A monster.

01:08:50.626 --> 01:08:52.378
That crazy bastard.

01:08:54.046 --> 01:08:55.047
Shall I

01:08:55.923 --> 01:08:57.091
just kill him?

01:08:58.676 --> 01:09:00.344
So, Park Ok-ran

01:09:00.928 --> 01:09:04.723
provoked Ko Dae-hwan
by humming "Oh My Darling, Clementine."

01:09:06.642 --> 01:09:07.852
Then, Ko Dae-hwan

01:09:08.978 --> 01:09:12.148
called her a monster
and tried to kill her.

01:09:12.231 --> 01:09:15.484
You can't fool me anymore, you monster!

01:09:17.653 --> 01:09:20.447
But the person he usually calls a monster

01:09:21.782 --> 01:09:23.367
is Do Hui-jae, his wife.

01:09:24.160 --> 01:09:25.161
Then,

01:09:26.203 --> 01:09:29.165
do you think
he mistook Ms. Park Ok-ran for his wife?

01:09:29.456 --> 01:09:31.834
Either she knows

01:09:33.127 --> 01:09:35.963
a lot about Do Hui-jae, or...

01:09:39.383 --> 01:09:42.970
Park Ok-ran could actually be Do Hui-jae.

01:09:59.737 --> 01:10:01.697
What brings you here?

01:10:02.656 --> 01:10:03.741
You said

01:10:05.409 --> 01:10:06.869
I could come over for food.

01:10:10.581 --> 01:10:13.334
Yes, I did. What would you like to eat?

01:10:30.059 --> 01:10:30.935
Happy birthday.

01:10:31.977 --> 01:10:33.312
It's not like you just gave birth,

01:10:33.395 --> 01:10:35.147
but you wanted to eat seaweed soup,

01:10:35.231 --> 01:10:36.523
so it must be your birthday.

01:10:37.441 --> 01:10:39.151
This is my birthday gift for you, then.

01:10:41.362 --> 01:10:42.571
Dig in.

01:10:54.833 --> 01:10:55.834
Do you like it?

01:10:58.379 --> 01:11:00.464
Well, it's not bad.

01:11:01.507 --> 01:11:02.549
I'm glad.

01:11:08.973 --> 01:11:10.266
Oh, boy.

01:11:28.951 --> 01:11:31.954
Hey, leave me alone.
Gosh, what a nuisance.

01:11:33.330 --> 01:11:34.540
Goodness, what the...

01:11:36.417 --> 01:11:39.336
Hey, you've been ignoring
all my calls and messages.

01:11:39.420 --> 01:11:40.963
Why the hell

01:11:41.547 --> 01:11:42.798
are you having dinner here?

01:11:42.881 --> 01:11:44.425
I said I'd buy you a steak--

01:11:44.508 --> 01:11:45.801
This seaweed soup has beef in it.

01:11:49.013 --> 01:11:51.807
Happy birthday, Ms. Ko.

01:11:52.057 --> 01:11:54.893
I'd like to sing a song
to celebrate Ms. Ko's birthday.

01:11:54.977 --> 01:11:56.353
Okay, sure.

01:11:58.355 --> 01:12:02.401
Why were you even born?

01:12:02.484 --> 01:12:04.528
You ugly

01:12:04.611 --> 01:12:05.779
Got a death wish?

01:12:22.379 --> 01:12:24.506
Damn it. That's the last one.

01:12:24.590 --> 01:12:27.468
I'll give you something
even more precious.

01:12:28.719 --> 01:12:31.347
Surprise! I got this for your birthday.

01:12:32.931 --> 01:12:35.976
They said this pendant
is two hearts put together,

01:12:36.060 --> 01:12:37.603
so I chose this in a heartbeat.

01:12:37.686 --> 01:12:39.396
Our hearts put together.

01:12:39.480 --> 01:12:41.273
It's perfect for us, isn't it?

01:12:41.357 --> 01:12:43.525
You write books, and I sell them.

01:12:53.452 --> 01:12:55.662
My gosh, it suits you perfectly.

01:12:55.746 --> 01:12:58.707
Oh, my.
You're dazzlingly beautiful, Mun-yeong.

01:12:58.791 --> 01:13:01.627
This is your way of pushing me
to get moving on my next book, isn't it?

01:13:01.710 --> 01:13:04.671
Okay, point taken.
I should get moving if you're pushing.

01:13:04.755 --> 01:13:06.256
Hey, what are you talking about?

01:13:11.303 --> 01:13:12.388
Mun-yeong.

01:13:15.849 --> 01:13:16.892
Hey, why are you--

01:13:16.975 --> 01:13:17.935
Stay there.

01:13:22.940 --> 01:13:25.734
Sang-tae, Moon Sang-tae! Open up, bestie.

01:13:25.818 --> 01:13:27.611
It's me. Open the door.

01:13:32.658 --> 01:13:34.785
No, no, I can't...

01:13:34.868 --> 01:13:37.162
If you don't let me in,
I'll break down the door.

01:13:39.248 --> 01:13:42.668
No, don't.
Don't break the door. Don't do that.

01:13:42.751 --> 01:13:45.629
I should... I should call the police.
What was the number?

01:13:45.712 --> 01:13:48.048
I brought a power saw. I'm not kidding.

01:13:48.924 --> 01:13:52.428
Gosh. Dial 911 to report a fire.

01:13:52.511 --> 01:13:53.929
Dial 111 to report a spy.

01:13:54.012 --> 01:13:56.765
- To report a crime...
- I can only wait three seconds.

01:13:56.849 --> 01:13:58.225
You'd better open up before that.

01:13:58.308 --> 01:13:59.560
- One.
- No...

01:13:59.643 --> 01:14:00.727
Two.

01:14:01.979 --> 01:14:03.897
- Three!
- Don't break it!

01:14:03.981 --> 01:14:05.399
Don't break down the door.

01:14:21.331 --> 01:14:23.250
- Here.
- Oh, Mang-tae.

01:14:24.793 --> 01:14:26.128
Take it back.

01:14:26.378 --> 01:14:27.254
I'm giving him up.

01:14:27.838 --> 01:14:28.672
You're giving him up?

01:14:29.756 --> 01:14:31.300
Instead of Mang-tae,

01:14:31.758 --> 01:14:32.593
can I have Sang-tae?

01:14:34.052 --> 01:14:35.804
I want Sang-tae.

01:14:41.518 --> 01:14:42.769
That smile is fake.

01:14:42.853 --> 01:14:45.898
No, it's real.
I'm bored without you, bestie.

01:14:47.733 --> 01:14:48.650
You're lying.

01:14:48.734 --> 01:14:50.235
I came to pick you up.

01:14:50.319 --> 01:14:51.570
You're lying.

01:14:52.154 --> 01:14:53.197
To tell you the truth,

01:14:54.448 --> 01:14:55.407
it's my birthday today--

01:14:55.491 --> 01:14:57.034
You're lying. You're lying to me.

01:14:57.117 --> 01:14:59.286
I want you to hang out with me,
as a birthday present.

01:14:59.369 --> 01:15:00.621
You're lying.

01:15:00.704 --> 01:15:02.623
Are you a lie detector or what?

01:15:02.706 --> 01:15:04.249
You're lying. Stop lying to me!

01:15:04.333 --> 01:15:06.460
You're lying!

01:15:06.543 --> 01:15:09.421
Liars are bad. Only bad people lie.

01:15:09.630 --> 01:15:12.341
Liar. She told me
she was going out by herself.

01:15:12.424 --> 01:15:13.467
All by herself.

01:15:13.550 --> 01:15:15.677
Besties don't keep secrets
from each other,

01:15:15.761 --> 01:15:18.013
but those two went somewhere fun
without me.

01:15:18.096 --> 01:15:20.098
I don't need this.

01:15:20.182 --> 01:15:21.558
I don't need a camping car anymore.

01:15:21.642 --> 01:15:24.478
I don't need a camping car.
I don't need this anymore!

01:15:24.686 --> 01:15:25.521
I don't need it!

01:15:55.050 --> 01:15:56.218
Sang-tae.

01:15:58.095 --> 01:15:59.930
The one who's really bad

01:16:01.431 --> 01:16:04.226
is the person who doesn't believe
anything others say.

01:16:04.977 --> 01:16:06.937
No, you're wrong. No.

01:16:08.313 --> 01:16:10.482
You know the story,
The Boy Who Cried Wolf, right?

01:16:11.858 --> 01:16:13.527
You don't look okay.

01:16:13.610 --> 01:16:15.904
Why don't you get an IV drip
instead of taking medicine?

01:16:16.071 --> 01:16:16.989
No, it's okay.

01:16:19.700 --> 01:16:20.617
This is enough.

01:16:20.701 --> 01:16:23.870
The shepherd boy lied all the time.

01:16:26.123 --> 01:16:29.918
The boy repeatedly lied to the villagers

01:16:30.419 --> 01:16:32.838
that a real wolf showed up.

01:16:35.716 --> 01:16:38.302
Do you know why the boy
tricked the villagers like that?

01:16:40.304 --> 01:16:42.556
Because he was bored, obviously.

01:16:43.056 --> 01:16:43.890
Wrong.

01:16:46.184 --> 01:16:47.352
Because he was lonely.

01:16:51.440 --> 01:16:54.860
He did that because he was so lonely,
all by himself in the mountains.

01:17:58.799 --> 01:18:01.551
- What happened?
- Ms. Park Ok-ran smacked him in the head.

01:18:01.635 --> 01:18:03.345
- What?
- Well...

01:18:03.929 --> 01:18:05.472
She said she dropped something important

01:18:05.555 --> 01:18:08.266
in the garden earlier
and asked me to help her find it,

01:18:08.350 --> 01:18:09.810
so I stepped out with her and--

01:18:09.893 --> 01:18:12.104
She suddenly grabbed a stone
and hit him in the head.

01:18:13.689 --> 01:18:15.440
He passed out and woke up just now.

01:18:17.150 --> 01:18:19.486
What about Ms. Park Ok-ran?
Where is she now?

01:18:19.569 --> 01:18:22.572
What do we do? It looks like she escaped.

01:18:22.656 --> 01:18:24.574
Call the police station nearby. Hurry.

01:18:24.658 --> 01:18:25.742
- Come with me.
- Okay.

01:18:26.868 --> 01:18:28.995
Anything else? Did she say anything else?

01:18:29.746 --> 01:18:31.581
She said today is
a very important day for her.

01:18:32.207 --> 01:18:34.876
I heard her mumbling about
having to meet someone today.

01:18:34.960 --> 01:18:36.586
Today is a very important day to me.

01:18:37.337 --> 01:18:38.839
- What if
- Did you get through?

01:18:38.922 --> 01:18:41.341
the writer Do Hui-jae actually isn't dead?

01:18:41.550 --> 01:18:43.218
- What if she just disappeared?
- Mr. Moon!

01:18:43.301 --> 01:18:45.095
- Then we know one thing for sure.
- No.

01:18:45.178 --> 01:18:46.805
- She'll definitely come back
- No.

01:18:46.888 --> 01:18:48.974
to see her husband and daughter.

01:18:49.057 --> 01:18:50.142
No!

01:18:55.147 --> 01:18:56.857
The shepherd boy

01:18:57.941 --> 01:18:59.943
lied because he was so lonely.

01:19:02.195 --> 01:19:04.740
But when a wolf actually appeared,

01:19:05.574 --> 01:19:07.784
no one came to help him.

01:19:10.495 --> 01:19:11.913
Had even just one person

01:19:13.749 --> 01:19:16.293
believed him and came to help him,

01:19:17.502 --> 01:19:19.588
the boy wouldn't have died.

01:19:49.326 --> 01:19:50.202
Ko Mun-yeong.

01:19:52.788 --> 01:19:53.830
Mun-yeong.

01:20:50.262 --> 01:20:51.346
I think...

01:20:52.180 --> 01:20:54.724
I'm finally living a normal life.

01:20:56.601 --> 01:20:58.562
You're an adult, right?

01:20:58.645 --> 01:21:01.690
An adult like Ko Gil-dong,
who can accept others as a family.

01:21:01.773 --> 01:21:04.150
- Gang-tae is mine.
- Gang-tae belongs to Gang-tae

01:21:04.234 --> 01:21:06.695
You can't have Gang-tae! Never!

01:21:06.778 --> 01:21:09.239
She had multiple plastic surgeries.

01:21:09.322 --> 01:21:10.740
She's been acting weird.

01:21:12.951 --> 01:21:15.537
I want a big brother like you!

01:21:17.956 --> 01:21:18.832
Gang-tae is...

01:21:19.332 --> 01:21:20.750
Happy.

01:21:21.334 --> 01:21:23.128
Gang-tae is happy.
